    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "bargauge",
      "title": "Top routes by request volume (5m rate)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "displayMode": "gradient",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "showUnfilled": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "topk(10, sum by (route) (rate(recon_api_http_requests_total{compose_project=\"$environment\", route!~\"/api/developer.*\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{route}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "topk over recon_api_http_requests_total. Excludes /api/developer/* -- those routes were removed months ago (Developer Dashboard re-architecture); historical Prometheus data from pre-#162 ZAP scans against them lives in the head block and can't be durably purged via delete_series until Prometheus's normal ~2h block-cutting cycle promotes it (confirmed live: delete_series+clean_tombstones appeared to work but reverted on container restart). apiMetrics.ts's /unmatched sentinel (Issue #167 follow-up) prevents any new unmatched-route noise going forward; this filter only needs to cover the one known-dead prefix that predates that fix."
    },
